# Episode 03 – Automated Calendar Event Creation

Once the confirmation email process was working, the next objective was to reduce the amount of manual scheduling work involved in managing client meetings.

In many businesses, receiving a meeting request is only the first step. Someone still needs to open a calendar, create an event, add client information, and make sure the meeting is scheduled correctly. As the number of appointments increases, this repetitive process becomes time-consuming and prone to human error.

To solve this problem, I integrated Google Calendar directly into the workflow.

When a qualified meeting request reaches the scheduling stage, n8n automatically creates a calendar event without any manual intervention. The event includes important information collected from the client form, such as meeting type, preferred date, contact details, and project information.

One important lesson from this episode was understanding how dynamic data moves between different nodes inside a workflow. I learned how to use expressions to pull information from previous steps and insert it into calendar events automatically.

Another key benefit of this automation is consistency. Every meeting is created using the same structure, which helps keep scheduling organized and professional.

From a business perspective, this removes a repetitive administrative task and allows more time to focus on client conversations instead of calendar management.

By the end of this episode, the workflow was capable of creating calendar events automatically whenever a meeting reached the scheduling stage.
